<title>USA: Transkaryotic Therapies says gets patent.</title>
<headline>Transkaryotic Therapies says gets patent.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transkaryotic Therapies Inc said  it was issued a European patent for gene therapy technology that changes  cells into delivery devices, able to bring virtually any therapeutic  protein to an affected cell for an extended period of time.</p>
<p>The company said the technology modify's a primary or normal cell's  DNA and allows it to carry the therapeutic protein to affected cells.   Transkaryotic said the patent also covers the site-specific insertion  of DNA (gene targeting) in normal cells.</p>
</text>
